{"id":"chatcmpl-05381c00-012b-434b-b27d-99e0cae4d968","object":"chat.completion","created":1795249028,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"```json\n{\n  \"highlights\": \"This task resolves a laterality question (left vs. right) in medical imaging where the answer depends on correctly mapping image coordinates to patient anatomy. The successful strategy combined independent expert/tool opinions, detected a conflict, and resolved it via direct visual inspection of an enlarged region of interest plus orientation-marker verification. The key abstraction is: when spatial laterality is ambiguous, triangulate multiple sources and confirm against patient-side conventions rather than trusting a single tool.\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"When a question hinges on spatial laterality (left/right), explicitly verify the image orientation marker before interpreting any side, since image-left often maps to patient-right.\",\n    \"Query at least two independent sources (expert tool + grounded report) for the same spatial attribute, and treat disagreement as a signal to escalate to direct inspection rather than picking one.\",\n    \"When tools conflict, resolve by zooming/cropping the specific region of interest and inspecting the original image directly, rather than re-querying the same tools.\",\n    \"Anchor the final answer to the patient-anatomy convention (e.g., 'convexity toward patient's right') and cross-check it against the independent report's phrasing.\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"Medical imaging interpretation\": \"Always confirm orientation/laterality markers first; use an expert descriptor and a grounded localization tool in parallel; escalate conflicts to a zoomed ROI crop of the original image.\",\n    \"Spatial/laterality QA tasks\": \"Distinguish image-coordinate side from subject-anatomy side; require an explicit mapping step before answering left/right questions.\",\n    \"Multi-tool conflict resolution\": \"Treat tool disagreement as a trigger for direct evidence inspection (crop/zoom/original), not majority voting among tools.\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Confirm the orientation marker and state the image-side to patient-side mapping before deciding left vs. right.\",\n    \"If two sources disagree on laterality, inspect an enlarged crop of the relevant region and cite the visual evidence in the final rationale.\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":620,"total_tokens":1053,"completion_tokens":433,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":620},"completion_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":433}}}